<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="S4.T2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Impact of KL<math id="S4.T2.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{prcp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">prcp</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{prcp}}</annotation></semantics></math> loss weighting.</span> Performance comparison on Qwen2.5-VL-3B trained with <span id="S4.T2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PAPO</span> using different values of <math id="S4.T2.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Increasing <math id="S4.T2.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> up to 0.02 generally improves performance, while an excessively large <math id="S4.T2.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> leads to model collapse (see detailed discussion in §<a href="#S5.SS4" title='5.4 Deep Dive on the KL_"prcp" Hacking ‣ 5 Results ‣ Perception-Aware Policy Optimization for Multimodal Reasoning' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>). The analysis of the effects of <math id="S4.T2.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> on 7B models are discussed in Figure <a href="#S5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Impact of Implicit Perception Loss weighting. ‣ 5.2 Ablation on Key Design Choices ‣ 5 Results ‣ Perception-Aware Policy Optimization for Multimodal Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
